# Musical Gustjumper: sing to the frogs on Zephras Isle (new in Forever).
# Sources: Forever's NPC data (the frogs, NPC 259005, on the rock; the Musical
# Gustjumper, NPC 259006, at 51.5,72.1 live); Forever's client data (item
# 268109: no binding, so it can be traded until used); beta reports (/sing at
# the rock, one frog hops onto the log, click it).
# INGAME: can a character who is not Skyborne ride the skyboat to Zephras Isle
# and see the frogs? (Two beta reports say anyone may visit; one says only
# Skyborne can reach the rock.)

step Skyboat from Dalaran
  only Alliance
  when !zone "Zephras Isle"
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Zephras Isle is the Skyborne starting island; by beta reports anyone may visit. A skyboat leaves the north side of Dalaran about every five minutes (another flies from north of Thunder Bluff; either faction may take either).
  goto 12.5,51.8 "Skyboat to Zephras Isle" live

step Skyboat from Thunder Bluff
  only Horde
  when !zone "Zephras Isle"
  zone Mulgore
  tip Zephras Isle is the Skyborne starting island; by beta reports anyone may visit. A skyboat leaves the cliffs south of Skywatcher Plateau, north of Thunder Bluff, about every five minutes (another flies from Dalaran; either faction may take either).
  goto 34.3,25.8 "Skyboat to Zephras Isle" live

step Sing to the frogs
  zone map 2521
  tip From Thendal Village follow the road south, then cut across the field to the top of the waterfall: five frogs sit together on a rock there, by a log. Mobs patrol nearby, so a level 1 character should watch its back. Stand by the rock, target a frog and type /sing. The frogs sing back, the group disappears and one frog hops onto the log beside you: click it to take the Musical Gustjumper, then use it to learn the pet. The item is not bound until you use it, so a friend on the island can sing again and trade you one.
  collect 268109 "Musical Gustjumper" @51.5,72.1 live
